Definition

Heap Pollution occurs when a variable of a parameterized (generic) type refers to an object that is actually of a different parameterized type.

In simple words:

The compiler thinks one type is stored in the heap, but the actual object is a different type.

How Can This Happen?

Normally Generics prevent this.

list.add(100);

Compiler immediately says

Error

So how does pollution happen?

Through

Raw Types
Arrays + Generics
Reflection
Unsafe casts